@file book/TPiL/Examples.lean
@decl TPiL.leanFirst
-- L4DEL: title: Elaborates Lean blocks first, maintaining the order of blocks
-- L4DEL: intuition: Elaborates Lean blocks first, maintaining the order of blocks. This makes their code available for `leanRef`.

@file book/TPiL/Examples.lean
@decl TPiL.logCommentMismatch
-- L4DEL: title: Reports a comment that doesn't describe the message its command produced
-- L4DEL: intuition: Reports a comment that doesn't describe the message its command produced. The corrected block is offered when the command occurs just once, so that replacing it is unambiguous. Any existing comment is dropped, which moves it to the place that suits the message.

@file book/TPiL/Examples.lean
@decl TPiL.messageComment?
-- L4DEL: title: Splits the marker that introduces a message off a comment's text, along with the severity it names, if any
-- L4DEL: intuition: Splits the marker that introduces a message off a comment's text, along with the severity it names, if any. A comment below a command describes the message it produces only when marked this way, which tells it apart from a comment that remarks on the code.

